# fixedbugs, defect 2036's finding, pinned 2026-10-13 as a known cost.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own whose `printf("%c\n", (bool)1)`
# hands `%c` a `bool` is refused `ffi_header_refused` at exit 1, `using '%c'
# format specifier, but argument has boolean value [-Werror,-Wformat]`.
#
# REASON: C defines the call: a `bool` argument is promoted to `int` (C11
# 6.5.2.2p6), which `%c` converts to `unsigned char` (7.21.6.1p8); but clang
# files the diagnostic under `-Wformat` itself, under none of its parts, and
# the region keeps `-Wformat` an error for the conversion its argument does
# not match, which reads the wrong bytes (defect 2034); no pragma reaches one
# of its own diagnostics alone (`emit/header_region.hero`).
#
# RULING: the author's, 2026-10-13, a known cost: robustness first (design.md
# §1.12). Revisit if clang gives this diagnostic a flag of its own; this
# golden moves when the region can pass it over.

extern "fixedbugs-2036-a-header-s-printf-of-a-bool-for-a-character-is-a-known-cost.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function fmt_shape() -> i32

function main()
    print(fmt_shape())
